1
00:03:51,818 --> 00:03:57,818
The mother of all movies.

2
00:07:43,636 --> 00:07:49,636
Hot Shots! is a action, comedy, war film directed by Jim Abrahams.

3
00:11:35,454 --> 00:11:41,454
The gang that created Airplane!

4
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
and The Naked Gun sets its sights on Top Gun in this spoof.

5
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:25,090
Topper Harley is a talented but unstable fighter pilot with
an axe to grind: clearing the family name.

6
00:23:10,909 --> 00:23:16,909
His mission is to avenge his father and save a mission
sabotaged by greedy weapons manufacturers.

7
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
He also gets involved in a relationship with Ramada Thompson,
a woman with an unusually talented stomach.

8
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
makes fun of a variety of other films, from Dances
with Wolves to The Fabulous Baker Boys.

9
00:34:46,363 --> 00:34:52,363
Topper Harley / Rhett Butler / Superman, played by Charlie Sheen.

10
00:38:38,181 --> 00:38:44,181
Kent Gregory, played by Cary Elwes.

11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Ramada Thompson / Scarlett O'Hara / Lois Lane, played by Valeria Golino.

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
Admiral Benson, played by Lloyd Bridges.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
Lt. Commander Block, played by Kevin Dunn.

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
Jim 'Wash Out' Pfaffenbach, played by Jon Cryer.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
is a 1991 American parody film directed by Jim Abrahams, co-writer and
co-director of Airplane!, and written by Abrahams and Pat Proft.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
It stars Charlie Sheen, Cary Elwes, Valeria Golino, Lloyd Bridges, Jon Cryer,
Kevin Dunn, Kristy Swanson, Bill Irwin, and Efrem Zimbalist Jr.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
The film is primarily a spoof of Top Gun, with some scenes spoofing other popular films, including 9½ Weeks, The
Fabulous Baker Boys, Dances with Wolves, Marathon Man, Rocky, Superman, First Blood, and Gone with the Wind.

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
A sequel, Hot Shots!

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
Part Deux, was released in 1993, with Sheen, Golino,
Bridges and Jerry Haleva reprising their roles.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of secret mission, bad luck,
parody, drill instructor, jet crash.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is lighthearted.
